# CeeLing fact pack: the part of the C++ standard library the compiler admits today.
#
# MIGRATED 2026-11-02 from the hand tables in library_summary.cpp with NO change in behaviour
# (tests/facts/ checks that every answer is the same). Everything here is hand-written, so
# source=declared review=hand. The plan is to replace the name lists by facts generated from the
# library's own declarations, with admission computed by rule (PLAN_third_party_inference.md,
# TODO.md "Third-party library facts"); until then this file is the whole of what `std` allows.
#
# Format (docs/internals/facts-format.md): one fact per line,
#     <kind> <subject> [flag ...] source=<declared|inferred> [review=<state>]
# Unknown kinds, unknown flags and a missing source= are load errors.
@pack std
@version 1
@origin hand-written, migrated from library_summary.cpp

# std::vector<T>. A name here may be called on a vector; `invalidates` = the call may reallocate or destroy
# elements, so every existing observer of the vector dies (CLAUDE.md threat #4); `shares-arg0` = the first
# argument is linked into the container, not consumed. `reserve` is on the invalidating list since 2026-11-02
# (the standard says a growing reserve invalidates references). `copyWithin` is CeeLing's own method, it has no
# std counterpart; `resize`, `reserve` and `copyWithin` are further limited to primitive elements by a language
# rule in escape_hatch_checker.cpp, which is policy, not a fact.
vector.method push_back invalidates shares-arg0 source=declared review=hand
vector.method pop_back invalidates source=declared review=hand
vector.method size source=declared review=hand
vector.method begin source=declared review=hand
vector.method end source=declared review=hand
vector.method resize invalidates source=declared review=hand
vector.method reserve invalidates source=declared review=hand
vector.method copyWithin source=declared review=hand

# std::string. `c_str` and `data` are deliberately absent: they extract a raw `const char*`, the escape-hatch
# shape CLAUDE.md's `.get()` ban closes. `invalidates` has no effect yet because a string observer is never
# registered (see TODO.md, "Fixed 2026-11-02").
string.method length source=declared review=hand
string.method size source=declared review=hand
string.method empty source=declared review=hand
string.method substr source=declared review=hand
string.method find source=declared review=hand
string.method append invalidates source=declared review=hand
string.method clear invalidates source=declared review=hand
string.method push_back invalidates source=declared review=hand
string.method reserve invalidates source=declared review=hand

# Free functions. `std::to_string`: number to text, returns a fresh string (nothing to borrow).
function std::stoi source=declared review=hand
function std::stod source=declared review=hand
function std::to_string source=declared review=hand
